          "tone": "paper",
          "title": "Tom Brown's Body",
          "copy": "For this true crime piece, the work leaned more into tone. I developed a series of moody, atmospheric animations that extend the feeling of the illustrations—letting moments linger, adding tension, and giving the visuals a sense of unease without overstating it.&#10;&#10;It was less about movement and more about pacing and restraint—helping set the emotional temperature of the story.",
